==English==

===Etymology===
From {{suffix|incident|al|lang=en}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ɪnsɪˈdɛntəl/|/ɪnsəˈdɛntəl/|lang=en}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# Loosely associated; existing as a [[byproduct]], [[tangent]], or [[accident]]; being a likely [[consequence]].
#: ''That character, though colorful, is '''incidental''' to the overall plot.''
# Occurring by chance
# {{lb|en|physics|of radiation}} Entering or approaching, prior to [[reflection]] (more frequently [[incident]]).

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|existing as an accident}} {{l|en|accidental}}, {{l|en|contingent}}; See also [[Thesaurus:circumstantial]]
* {{sense|occurring by chance}} {{l|en|accidental}}, {{l|en|serendipitous}}; See also [[Thesaurus:accidental]]

====Antonyms====
* {{sense|existing as an accident}} {{l|en|inevitable}}, {{l|en|necessary}}, {{l|en|impossible}}; See also [[Thesaurus:inevitable]]
* {{sense|occurring by chance}} {{l|en|inevitable}}, {{l|en|intentional}}; See also [[Thesaurus:intentional]]

